++HOLD (FSD0217) FMID(CTSA400) SYSTEM REASON(DELETE)
 COMMENT
 (
BEMD#BDEL
  This PTF deletes the LMOD(s) listed below, therefore it will be
  impossible to restore this PTF. Please ensure that sufficient
  backups exist.

       LMOD(s) list:
       -------------
$1   LMOD        CTSAPCC
$1   LMOD        CTSAP84
$1   LMOD        CTSCACD
$1   LMOD        CTSCACS
$1   LMOD        CTSCDIAG
$1   LMOD        CTSCGRO
$1   LMOD        CTSCOFL
$1   LMOD        CTSCONI
 )
 .
++HOLD (FSD0217) FMID(CTSA400) SYSTEM REASON(ACTION)
 COMMENT
 (
BEMD#BBKP
  Prior to APPLYing this PTF, please verify that the member(s) listed
  below were not modified locally and that you have an updated BACKUP
  of the library.

       TYPE        ELEMENT         LIBRARY
       ----        -------         -------
$1   PROC        CTSAONI         PROCLIB
$1   SAMP        CTSPARMJ        INSTALL
     . . . . . .
BEMD#ATLR
  After applying the PTF submit the S8TAILOR job from the UPGRADE
  library to tailor all updated elements according to the values
  specified during MF Connector installation.

  Re-apply local modificatins, if any.

       TYPE        ELEMENT         LIBRARY
       ----        -------         -------
$1   PROC        CTSAONI         PROCLIB
$1   SAMP        CTSPARMJ        INSTALL
     . . . . . .
BEMD#ASAE
  After APPLYing this fix, EXITs used by the online interceptor should
  be re-compiled and set in the system.  This refers to all EXITs used
  by online interceptor:

  TSS installation EXIT
  RACF SMF EXIT, 2 password EXITs and phassphrase EXIT
  ACF2 SMF EXIT, password EXIT and passphrase EXIT

  Please refer to MF Connector Administrator Guide for detailed
  explanations how to install the relevant EXIT/s used by the online
  interceptor.
     . . . . . .
BEMD#APCP
  After successfully APPLYing the PTF, copy (and rename if required)
  the procedure elements listed below to the site's PROCLIB Library,
  which is pointed to by the %PROCLIB% parameter of the DEFPARMS
  member in the INSTALL library.

  Re-apply local modifications, if exist, to these elements, before
  restarting the MF Connector.

       TYPE        ELEMENT         LIBRARY
       ----        -------         -------
$1   PROC        CTSAONI         PROCLIB
 )
 .
